                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7fc5b005-4c1a-3440-976e-df6cddd22d4d",
                        "entry_id": "7a8c4390-b514-3517-abdd-514fab6c6123",
                        "glosses": [
                            "презр. поведение, поступки двурушника; стремление одновременно действовать в пользу двух противоположных сторон"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "251f0f6f-a4f6-40de-b0c4-63d39617540c",
                                "sense_id": "7fc5b005-4c1a-3440-976e-df6cddd22d4d",
                                "text": "Ни шахтинцы, ни «промпартийцы» не доходили до таких геркулесовых столбов цинизма, коварства, лицемерия и двурушничества, до каких дошли троцкисты."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a9fb395-c6ba-4c42-aa84-e37cb90cff9f",
                                "sense_id": "7fc5b005-4c1a-3440-976e-df6cddd22d4d",
                                "text": "Очень часто можно наблюдать: человеческая мать обнаруживает склонность подчиняться только законам природы, но в то же время не отказывается от благ человеческой культуры. Как можно назвать такое поведение? Только двурушничеством."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a5525b98-0a8f-4401-b5f3-268f189b5740",
                                "sense_id": "7fc5b005-4c1a-3440-976e-df6cddd22d4d",
                                "text": "Мы помогаем и властям, и церкви околпачивать народ — и оттого двурушничество искусства, его зависимость достигли небывалых размеров, неслыханной развязности и наглого самодовольства."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b13bd9c1-f8e1-45d3-89ca-9337658b5faa",
                        "source_entry_id": "7a8c4390-b514-3517-abdd-514fab6c6123",
                        "source_sense_id": "7fc5b005-4c1a-3440-976e-df6cddd22d4d",
                        "target_lang_word": "double-dealing",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "double-dealing",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "84174c27-11e6-3ba4-87db-8e45cc6948f8",
                                        "entry_id": "9410ba97-618e-3dec-84ab-01917e23e557",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Cheating, dishonest; treacherous."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8411dd1-eb46-4aab-9225-f904d8c0df22",
                                                "sense_id": "84174c27-11e6-3ba4-87db-8e45cc6948f8",
                                                "text": "You low-down, no-good, double-dealing sidewinder!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "double-dealing",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e327ed15-c04c-300f-bc85-395832259b1b",
                                        "entry_id": "1a574219-7e02-3ac9-9c16-584804ea8d5c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "deceit or treachery"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1397af96-0246-4e0a-8232-00dbd12c37b0",
                        "source_entry_id": "7a8c4390-b514-3517-abdd-514fab6c6123",
                        "source_sense_id": "7fc5b005-4c1a-3440-976e-df6cddd22d4d",
                        "target_lang_word": "deceit",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "deceit",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e62ff7b8-8ba9-386b-b8ca-d3e269b0e008",
                                        "entry_id": "0e4cf68a-73a5-3fb2-819f-1450a7cb87b1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An act or practice intended to deceive; a trick."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2790701d-0493-4467-acc2-b1e835c0d74b",
                                                "sense_id": "e62ff7b8-8ba9-386b-b8ca-d3e269b0e008",
                                                "text": "The whole conversation was merely a deceit."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "96931005-8db7-3a81-b766-d097550f1f56",
                                        "entry_id": "0e4cf68a-73a5-3fb2-819f-1450a7cb87b1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An act of deceiving someone."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d6d0d6b-ae08-4327-8ef2-7c6768e7f223",
                                                "sense_id": "96931005-8db7-3a81-b766-d097550f1f56",
                                                "text": "Upon his return he killed Eriphyle for her vanity and deceit of him and his father."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "113fbae6-66ad-39c9-8353-931726517bf1",
                                        "entry_id": "0e4cf68a-73a5-3fb2-819f-1450a7cb87b1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being deceitful or deceptive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e3a58f9-7f95-4a08-a826-abc70b30e07f",
                                                "sense_id": "113fbae6-66ad-39c9-8353-931726517bf1",
                                                "text": "[T]he tvvo commended rules by him [Aristotle] ſet down, vvhereby the axioms of Sciences are precepted to be made convertible, and vvhich the latter men have not vvithout elegancy ſurnamed; the one the rule of truth, becauſe it preventeth deceipt; the other the rule of prudence, becauſe it freeth election, are the ſame thing in ſpeculation and affirmation, vvhich vve novv obſerve."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea35b5ba-b222-4d49-8545-a5f85e99618e",
                                                "sense_id": "113fbae6-66ad-39c9-8353-931726517bf1",
                                                "text": "His mouth is full of curſing, and deceit, and fraud : vnder his tongue is miſchiefe and vanitie."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d6f0d8c4-8311-3986-ae3e-df267aef750b",
                                        "entry_id": "0e4cf68a-73a5-3fb2-819f-1450a7cb87b1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The tort or fraudulent representation of a material fact made with knowledge of its falsity, or recklessly, or without reasonable grounds for believing its truth and with intent to induce reliance on it; the plaintiff justifiably relies on the deception, to his injury."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "70cd6764-e30f-46b2-9e8d-ed1e9d8fdc7e",
                        "source_entry_id": "7a8c4390-b514-3517-abdd-514fab6c6123",
                        "source_sense_id": "7fc5b005-4c1a-3440-976e-df6cddd22d4d",
                        "target_lang_word": "treachery",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "treachery",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "064095ea-c8df-3f3a-a2be-5003241f0193",
                                        "entry_id": "f60c7936-a8ca-384e-a4fa-dc1f5694100a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Deliberate, often calculated, disregard for trust or faith."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c314b71c-a56e-4763-85d2-bceaae6aaa42",
                                                "sense_id": "064095ea-c8df-3f3a-a2be-5003241f0193",
                                                "text": "Suddenly, in the midst of high-camp treachery and sleuthery, each character does a star turn, breaking out in song."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6b68066a-2899-3b88-8f87-446be259e44f",
                                        "entry_id": "f60c7936-a8ca-384e-a4fa-dc1f5694100a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of violating the confidence of another, usually for personal gain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "05ced43e-c308-3c38-a45d-9f2732d81ba4",
                                        "entry_id": "f60c7936-a8ca-384e-a4fa-dc1f5694100a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Treason."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9a7dfb29-82aa-31d2-b340-59f4735f75df",
                                        "entry_id": "f60c7936-a8ca-384e-a4fa-dc1f5694100a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An act or instance of treachery."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e1f26cd-f8c3-43d7-9aa6-fa69d90c4f74",
                                                "sense_id": "9a7dfb29-82aa-31d2-b340-59f4735f75df",
                                                "text": "These submerged treacheries left an atmosphere. Even two such practised obliterators of their species as Bradly and Podson could not fail to note that each was secreting a certain reservation of opinion on the other."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
